                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "76ba7a1f-e930-35ca-8f9b-06797ac57b4b",
                        "entry_id": "920b0439-f13d-3a7a-a5cf-323eef8f51bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "архит. архитектурная деталь дорического ордера: узкий выпуклый профиль, идущий сверху архитрава и отделяющий его от фриза"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40eb9d45-8123-486f-97ee-260be2ff594c",
                                "sense_id": "76ba7a1f-e930-35ca-8f9b-06797ac57b4b",
                                "text": "С нижней стороны тении под каждым триглифом имелась еще небольшая полочка, так называемая регула, равная по длине ширине триглифа."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "049c2ac3-4e92-4da8-bdf5-712b6f6e6640",
                        "source_entry_id": "920b0439-f13d-3a7a-a5cf-323eef8f51bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "76ba7a1f-e930-35ca-8f9b-06797ac57b4b",
                        "source_sense_description": "архитектурная деталь дорического ордера",
                        "target_lang_word": "T-adapter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4eb14bc5-4b6f-473b-8943-fd9fa56ae8c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "920b0439-f13d-3a7a-a5cf-323eef8f51bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "76ba7a1f-e930-35ca-8f9b-06797ac57b4b",
                        "source_sense_description": "архитектурная деталь дорического ордера",
                        "target_lang_word": "taenia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "taenia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07ab7ecc-9050-3f4e-8c24-72fb88454575",
                                        "entry_id": "c0656240-2165-37a2-8545-8d226c9e389f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ribbon worn in the hair in ancient Greece."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3602ff9a-3d6d-47ac-94ae-9d82ae81c2cd",
                                                "sense_id": "07ab7ecc-9050-3f4e-8c24-72fb88454575",
                                                "text": "Taenia and ivy leaves are added by hand. Figure wears a taenia horizontally over her brow and a spray of ivy in her hair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a6181b4-9df4-306c-9149-a6857d14e989",
                                        "entry_id": "c0656240-2165-37a2-8545-8d226c9e389f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A band between the frieze and architrave in the Doric order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Doric"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a7c5c61-f754-42a3-a81a-db76ed0a391c",
                                                "sense_id": "5a6181b4-9df4-306c-9149-a6857d14e989",
                                                "text": "2004, William Bell Dinsmoor, The Propylaia to the Athenian Acropolis, Volume 2: The Classical Building, page 165,\nThe height of the taenia was likewise determined with regard to the total height of the epistyle, and again, although we should not expect a proportion of less than one-twelfth of the total height (as in the Parthenon), it is reduced to one-thirteenth, executed as 0.089-0.090 m."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "336f11dc-4c5b-358b-85fe-4083a77bf685",
                                        "entry_id": "c0656240-2165-37a2-8545-8d226c9e389f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several ribbon-like bands of tissue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "888eef88-4fe6-430a-b1fe-b517eaa707f7",
                                                "sense_id": "336f11dc-4c5b-358b-85fe-4083a77bf685",
                                                "text": "The taenia selected will generally be the so-called omental taenia, from which the greater omentum arises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99d825ce-8c34-42d5-8d7c-04c9378fcdb2",
                                                "sense_id": "336f11dc-4c5b-358b-85fe-4083a77bf685",
                                                "text": "Each taenia traverses one of the following surfaces of the colon: the anterior surface, the posteroinferior surface, and the posterosuperior surface."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76575087-509d-45df-96be-c41a335e3e98",
                                                "sense_id": "336f11dc-4c5b-358b-85fe-4083a77bf685",
                                                "text": "The general characteristics of the colon are its large caliber; the presence of pendant-shaped bodies of fat enclosed by peritoneum, called omental appendices; and the longitudinal muscle in its walls, which forms three narrow, ribbon-like bands called taeniae coli. The locations of the taeniae are useful landmarks and are specific in relation to the position of the colon itself. The posterior taenia, or tenia omental, is found on the posterolateral border of the ascending and descending colons and the anterior border of the transverse colon. The anterior taenia, or tenia libera,[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "001e90ae-1681-43c0-aff5-3a952d5691be",
                                                "sense_id": "336f11dc-4c5b-358b-85fe-4083a77bf685",
                                                "text": "The choroid plexus is attached medially to the body of the fornix by the taenia fornicis and laterally to the thalamus by the taenia choroidea. The taenia is actually a continuation of the ependyma that covers the ventricular cavity over the choroid plexus of the lateral ventricle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "529a35c7-d849-3287-986b-07b9ac84911e",
                                        "entry_id": "c0656240-2165-37a2-8545-8d226c9e389f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any species of the genus Taenia of tapeworms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "726646ec-3ed0-4e5d-b012-aa16654925a4",
                                                "sense_id": "529a35c7-d849-3287-986b-07b9ac84911e",
                                                "text": "About an hour after the last dose, that is, in three hours after commencing the remedy, an entire tænia was voided alive, no other effect than a slight nausea having been experienced by the patient.[…]On plunging living tæniae either into the decoction, or into the mixture of the pomegranate bark and water, they writhe and manifest great suffering."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
